{"id": "z1010", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, let's think about this. A corpse would typically be covered by a blanket in a place where it is stored or kept after death. Let' s look at the options. A bath store sounds like a place for selling bath products, not really appropriate for that. A bedroom could happen if someone passed away there, but it's usually temporary before removal. A hospital often handles the initial care and may cover bodies briefly, but they don't keep them long-term. A flower garden isn't a storage place. Michigan is just a state, too broad. The most logical place to store a body covered with a blanket is in a morgue or mortuary, which is part of a hospital or funeral home setting. So while none of these are perfect, the best fit is probably C, hospital, because many hospitals have mortuaries where bodies are temporarily held.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 45, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1018", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "An underrated thing about computers is how they manage workflow. At one time, it was a big deal when they could first do arithmetic. That' s B.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 8, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1026", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "According to many religious traditions, God will never do anything. This is because it is believed that God is all-powerful and capable of doing anything. However, there are some things that are considered impossible for God to do, such as sinning or lying. In addition, some religions teach that God does not intervene in human affairs except under certain circumstances.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1034", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Athletes soak in hot tubs to relieve sore muscles after playing baseball. The heat from the hot water helps relax tense muscles and reduce inflammation, making it easier to recover after a game or practice.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
