{"id": "z1074", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Since he was a sloppy eater, the mess would likely be left at his dining area. Of the options given, a desk is where one typically eat s if they don't have a dedicated dining table or space. So the answer should be B: desk.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1082", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The man started to learn jogging, what was he hoping to do? A. exhaust ion B. getting in shape C. fitness D. injure himself E. fatigue I think the most likely answer is B. getting in shape or C. fitness. These are common reasons people start jo gging.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1090", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Billy was reading the newspaper as he comm uted to work, but once he got to his destination, he ball ed it up and put it somewhere. Where did he put it? A trash, C sub way, D ground, or E lawn ? It's most likely trash. People usually don't leave crumpled newspaper s lying around subways, grounds, or law ns when they get to their destinations. The most logical place for him to dispose of it would be in the trash can.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 33, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1098", "pool": "know-commonsense", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "I would say the ideal location for a post office is E, center of town. The center of town is usually where most people live and work, making it convenient for everyone to access postal services like sending letters or packages. While options like A, B, C, and D might be practical in some cases, they often aren't as central or accessible as the town center.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1106", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 15, "onset_chunk": 14, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D, contain their necessary nutrition. When a farmer harvests seeds from plants like tomatoes and save s them for later planting, those seeds already have the genetic information needed to grow into new plants. They carry the nutrients and instructions required to develop once they are planted in soil with water and light. While dirt and sunlight are essential for growth, the seeds themselves do not need extra dirt or sun just to exist; they simply require those elements to ger minate and thrive.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 28, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1114", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D. A recycl able material can be used more times. Recycl ing means processing waste materials to make new products, so the main purpose of rec ycling is to reuse resources. This helps save raw materials and reduce environmental impact.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1122", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 4, "onset_chunk": 3, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Predators eat A, lions. They' re carnivores that hunt other animals for food.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 5, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1130", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, it really depends on the context. If we're talking about cutting through hard materials like metal or wood, an iron saw would likely last longer because of its strength and durability. Alumin ium saws might be lighter but not as durable for heavy duty tasks. Pla stic and wooden saws are generally more fragile and could wear out faster when used in demanding situations. So overall, I would say the iron saw is probably your best bet for lasting longer.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1138", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Jupiter has more gravity force than Earth but less than the Sun.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1146", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A mola mo la might live in the Bay of Ben gal. These fish are typically found in warm, tropical waters around the world. The Bay of Bengal has suitable conditions for them to thrive.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1154", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A dog is warm- blooded just like a cardinal. That's the right answer.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1162", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Cold-blooded animals are often slow. Their activity levels depend on the temperature of their environment, so they tend to move slower when it's cold and faster when it's warm.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1170", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A bat starts its life similarly to a chicken. Both are born from eggs and undergo a similar early development process, unlike pig s or butterflies which have very different lifecycles.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1178", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Respiration is a common ality among all animals. So the correct answer is D. It happens for some species, but not just land dwelling mammals or sea creatures. All animals need to breathe in oxygen and expel carbon dioxide, so it's universal across the animal kingdom.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 14, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1186", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Dunes can be made out of the same thing as A, clothes.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 4, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1194", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Aluminum is a re processable material. It' s not plastic, nor is it a liquid absorb ent. It can be melted down and reused over and over again without losing quality, making it very eco- friendly in many applications.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1202", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Mammals give birth to live young, unlike birds, which lay eggs. This is one of the key differences between mam mals and most other animals like fish or insect s that reproduce by laying eggs.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1210", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 6, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Earth revolves around the sun, which is located in outer space. So while outer space isn' t technically an object that Earth orbits, it's where this movement takes place. The correct answer is B, outer space.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 11, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1218", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 6, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D, nasal de congestants. When used for extended periods or in high doses, they can lead to rebound congestion and other issues like increased blood pressure or heart problems.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 5, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1226", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 7, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The Great Lakes are thought to have been formed by a combination of glaciation and volcanic activity, particularly during the last ice age. While they were not directly formed by a single volcano, their shape s and surrounding land forms were influenced by ancient volcanic regions in North America. So while not a direct result of a volcan o, the geological history includes significant vol canic influence.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1234", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The best option is B, kitchen foil. It can reflect light well, making you more visible to drivers at night.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 7, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1242", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 5, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Camouflage can be used by animals for hunting water, trees, air, or meals.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 6, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1250", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B, eight boxes. A Punnett square used to determine the percent chance of a trait being passed down typically has at least eight box es when considering mono geneic traits in diploid organisms like humans. It' s set up as a 2x4 grid or similar configuration depending on the number of alleles involved, allowing for the calculation of genetic probabilities between parents and offspring.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1258", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 5, "onset_chunk": 4, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "In order to catch a rabbit, the predator needs to be quick. Ra bbits are fast and can run away easily, so being quick helps the predator catch it before it escapes. So the answer is B, quick.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 13, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1266", "pool": "know-openbook", "n_q_chunks": 8, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Earthquakes are only happening in California? No, that's not true. E arthquakes happen all over the world, especially along plate boundaries. Do they cause solar and lunar eclipses? No way. E clips es are caused by the alignment of the Sun, Moon, and Earth. Will they break your v ases? Probably, if they're on a shelf during strong shaking. And do they make bridges safer? Not at all. They can actually damage bridges unless they' re specifically designed to handle seismic activity.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 28, "carrier_ended": null}
