{"id": "z1714", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 15, "onset_chunk": 15, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "There are now 21 orchids and 2 2 roses in the vase. To find how many more roses than or chids there are, we subtract the number of orchids from the number of roses. So, 2 2 minus 2 1 equals 1. Therefore, there is 1 more rose than or chid in the vase now.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1722", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The machine made 1 2 0 shirts yesterday and 8 4 today, for a total of 2 04 shirt s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 9, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1730", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 10, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "He started with 21 books. He bought 4 2 new ones, but now has only 15 in total. Let's figure out how many he must have sold. If we add his current 15 to the 42 he bought, that gives us 57. Since he originally had 2 1, he must have sold 3 6 books. Now, comparing that to the 4 2 he bought, he sold 6 fewer books than he bought.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1738", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 13, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Two children were riding on the bus. At the bus stop, some more children got on the bus. Then there were ten children altogether on the bus. So we start with two children on the bus before the stop. After the stop, there are ten children in total. To find out how many more children got on at the stop, we sub tract the original number from the final number. That is ten minus two, which equal s eight. Therefore, eight more children are on the bus now than there were before the bus stop.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1746", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 13, "onset_chunk": 12, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Paul got a box of 65 crayons for his birthday. During the school year, he gave 213 crayons to his friends and lost 1 6 more. So we add those two numbers together: 2 13 plus 16 equal s 22 9. That means Paul had given away or lost a total of 2 29 crayon s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 19, "carrier_ended": null}
