{"id": "z1874", "pool": "easy-mathword", "n_q_chunks": 17, "onset_chunk": 16, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "If there were 8 9 bird families living near the mountain and 60 flew away for winter, then we need to find out how many stayed behind. Let ’s subtract the number that left from the total. So 8 9 minus 60 equal s 29. That means 29 bird families stayed. Now, to find out how many more flew away than stayed, we sub tract the number that stayed from those that went. So 60 minus 2 9 equal s 31. Therefore, 3 1 more bird families flew away for the winter than those that stayed behind.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 34, "carrier_ended": null}
