{"id": "z1938", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 16, "onset_chunk": 15, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is B, Chicxulub Crater on the Yucat an Peninsula in Mexico. This massive impact crater was formed by a huge asteroid or comet that struck Earth about 65 million years ago, which is widely believed to have caused the mass extinction event that wiped out the di nosaurs and many other species. While Tunguska in Siber ia involved a much smaller air burst explosion, and Meteor Crater in Arizona is much smaller and younger, none of these are linked to the dinosaur extinction.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z1946", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "For 9 9% of human history, people have depended solely on foraging. Before agriculture was developed, humans gathered plants, hunted animals, and collected other resources from their environment to survive. So the correct answer is D: foraging.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
