{"id": "z1962", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 21, "onset_chunk": 20, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, let's think about it. Before humans started farm ing, they mainly gathered food from nature without changing the environment much. But when people began to grow their own crops and raise animals, that was a big change. The Neolithic Re volution marked the start of this shift to controlled agriculture. So if we look at the timeline, farming really took off around 10, 000 years ago. That places it firmly within the past 12, 000 years. So the answer is B.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 28, "carrier_ended": null}
