{"id": "z2146", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The answer is D, learning and memory. Long- term potentiation plays a critical role in learning and memory. It refers to the strengthening of synap tic connections between neurons, which is believed to be a cellular mechanism underlying the formation and storage of memories. While it may have some influence on emotional processes, its primary association is with learning and memory.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2154", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 9, "onset_chunk": 8, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The answer is C, both A and B. Ed dy current losses occur when a conduct ing material like iron is exposed to a changing magnetic field. This induces circulating currents within the metal itself, which generate heat and energy loss. Hysteres is losses happen because of the resistance of the material to changes in magnet ic domains as it is magnetized or demagnetized during operation. By using thin laminations separated by an insulating layer, you interrupt these currents and reduce hysteresis effects, thus lowering both types of losses.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 20, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2162", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 16, "onset_chunk": 15, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "A psychologist who believes development occurs in stages is most interested in the controversy between continuity and discontinu ity. This debate centers on whether development is a smooth progression or happens through distinct stages. Someone focusing on stages would argue for dis continuities, meaning clear changes at specific points rather than gradual shifts. So the correct answer is B, continuity versus discontinu ity.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 25, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2170", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 11, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is D. All of the above. Shunt cap acitors, series capacitors, and generation excitation control are all used for reactive or voltage compensation in power systems. Each method serves a specific purpose to help maintain stable voltage levels across the grid.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 16, "carrier_ended": null}
