{"id": "z2226", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 12, "onset_chunk": 11, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is C. Threat. This question assess es your understanding of external factors that could negatively impact the organization's performance. A threat refers to potential risks or challenges from outside sources, such as market competition, economic downturn s, regulatory changes, or technological disruptions. These elements are considered threats because they can undermine stability and hinder performance.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 18, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2234", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 35, "onset_chunk": 34, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "To create the most efficient audit when an audit client uses a service organization for several processes, you should review the service auditor's report on controls placed in operations and outline the accounting system in a memo to the working papers. This approach allows the user audit or to leverage the findings of the service auditor while document ing how those control s are integrated into the client's accounting systems. It streamlines the audit process by avoid ing redundant testing of controls already evaluated by the service auditor, making it more efficient without compromising the quality of the audit evidence.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 34, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2242", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 31, "onset_chunk": 7, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "It uses the following performance optimizationT o represent numbers in a special way, and constant time implementation to prevent timing attacks. The repeated squaring algorithm is used for exponent ial operations.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 10, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2250", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 10, "onset_chunk": 9, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Productivity is usually the most valid objective criteria for assessing job performance because it directly reflects an employee's contribution to organizational goals. While other factors like absences or accidents may indicate issues, they don't necessarily measure actual work output or effectiveness.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 17, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2258", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 24, "onset_chunk": 23, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The statement that is not true is D. The time it takes for the Moon to make one circuit of our sky is not one solar day. A solar day refers to the time it takes for the Sun to return to the same position in the sky, which is approximately 2 4 hours. In contrast, the Mo on completes a full orbit around Earth roughly every 27.3 days, known as a sidereal month, which is much longer than a so lar day.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2266", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 14, "onset_chunk": 14, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "Well, if we're talking about the combination of reinforce rs and punish ers, that's really a hallmark of behavior al psychology. So I think you can pretty much rule out William James, who was more interested in consciousness and how our minds work. Wilhelm Wundt is also going to be more focused on things like introspec tion, which is looking inside yourself. Carl Roger s was very much into humanistic psychology, so he would focus more on self- actualization. But when it comes to re inforcers and punishers, B F Skinner is your guy. He's all about operant conditioning, where you look at what happens after a behavior and whether it gets reinforced or punish ed. So the answer here is definitely C, B F Skinner.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 32, "carrier_ended": null}
