{"id": "z2290", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 34, "onset_chunk": 34, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "So when a child is frightened by the barking of a neighbor' s dog, her sympathetic nervous system kicks in, causing her heart rate to rise and stress hormones like adrena line to surge. But once her mother picks her up and she begins to calm down, it ’s because the parasympath etic nervous system takes over again. This system counter acts the fight-or-flight responses that were triggered earlier. It helps slow things down—reducing heart rate, relax ing muscles, and bringing the body back to a resting state. So the correct answer is A: the para sympathetic nervous system resumes control and reverses the sympathetic response s.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 35, "carrier_ended": null}
{"id": "z2298", "pool": "know-mmlu", "n_q_chunks": 15, "onset_chunk": 14, "no_speak": false, "answer_text": "The correct answer is A. To ga viruses are en veloped spherical particles with an icos ahedral structure. They have a lipid envelope derived from the host cell, which helps them enter and exit host cells. Their genetic material is single- stranded RNA, packed inside a protein shell that forms an icosahedron. This shape allows efficient packing of the genome. Examples include the virus es responsible for West Nile fever and chikungunya.", "eot_seen": true, "n_ans_chunks": 22, "carrier_ended": null}
